I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`. Adding an `http-client` import would widen that grant, and the approval in the request doesn't change the declared grant. Building the URL from the raw input text would also send that text to an external host unencoded, which is a separate problem. The code below implements the clock-only node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

